.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-SECURE-BOOT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-secure-boot
.Nd sign what kldload builds with the machine's own key, and have the firmware's shim trust it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | enable | disable | reenroll
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With Secure Boot on, the firmware boots Microsoft-signed shim, and shim
boots only what is signed by a key it trusts: the distribution's, or a
machine owner key enrolled by someone at the console in MokManager.
kldload's ZFS module and ZFSBootMenu are built on the machine, so they
are signed on the machine, with the root key of its certificate authority,
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
which is enrolled as a machine owner key.
.Pp
.Nm
turns that on after an install that did not, reports on it, and turns
module signing off.
It never changes the firmware's own Secure Boot setting.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
The firmware's Secure Boot state, the authority's root certificate, whether
that certificate is enrolled or waiting to be, which key signed the ZFS
module on disk, and whether DKMS is set to sign modules it builds.
Needs no root.
.It Cm enable
Needs root.
In order: makes the authority if there is none; copies its root key and
certificate to
.Pa /var/lib/dkms/mok.key ,
.Pa mok.pub
and
.Pa mok.der ;
sets DKMS to sign every module it builds with them; signs the ZFS module
on disk now if it is an uncompressed
.Pa .ko
\(em a compressed one, as Fedora ships, is left for DKMS to sign when it
next builds it, since signing it in place would corrupt it; signs
ZFSBootMenu on the EFI partition, replacing any
signature it had; and queues the certificate for enrolment, unless it is
enrolled or queued already.
The next boot stops in MokManager: choose
.Dq Enroll MOK ,
give the password, and reboot.
Then Secure Boot can be turned on in the firmware.
.Pp
Any EFI binary that carries a Microsoft signature is shim and is left
alone.
.It Cm disable
Needs root.
Takes back a queued enrolment, if the password matches, and removes the
DKMS signing configuration, so modules built after this are not signed.
The authority, an enrolled key, and modules already signed stay.
.It Cm reenroll
Needs root.
Queues the certificate for enrolment again \(em after a
.Dq \&No
in MokManager, or after the firmware's variables were cleared.
Signs nothing.
.It Fl h , Fl -help , Cm help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_MOK_PASSWORD
The one-time password MokManager asks for; default
.Ql kldload .
One set here is not printed.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_ESP
The EFI partition's mount point, instead of
.Pa /boot/efi ;
for testing against a copy.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.key , Pa ca.crt , Pa ca.der
The authority's root key and certificate.
.It Pa /var/lib/dkms/mok.key , Pa mok.pub , Pa mok.der
The copies DKMS signs with; the key mode 0600.
.It Pa /etc/dkms/framework.conf.d/kldload-mok.conf , Pa /etc/dkms/sign_helper.sh
DKMS's signing configuration and helper.
.It Pa /boot/efi/EFI/zbm/BOOTX64.EFI
ZFSBootMenu, signed; older installs also at
.Pa EFI/kldload/ .
.It Pa /boot/efi/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
Shim, or ZFSBootMenu on a machine without shim; signed only in the second
case.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done.
.It 1
Not root, or a step failed.
.It 2
No command, or an unknown one.
.El
.Pp
A failure to queue the enrolment inside
.Cm enable
is reported and does not change its exit status.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss A desktop
Printed on 2026-09-30:
